\title{researchreproducibility: reproducibility audits of projects and articles}
\description{
Two kinds of audit, both describing \emph{conditions} for reproducibility, not
whether a result was reproduced:
}
\details{
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=rr_audit]{rr_audit()}}: a project directory, against the checklist in
\code{\link[=rr_checklist]{rr_checklist()}};
\item \code{\link[=rr_detect]{rr_detect()}}: the full text of articles, with the transparency detectors
of the REPRO2IMPACT study (detector version 1.1.0).
}

Results use four statuses: \code{met}, \code{not_met}, \code{not_applicable} and
\code{unverifiable}. Something that cannot be checked is \code{unverifiable}, never
\code{not_met}. \code{\link[=rr_report]{rr_report()}} and \code{\link[=rr_write_json]{rr_write_json()}} write the results;
\code{\link[=rr_template]{rr_template()}} and \code{\link[=rr_use_github_action]{rr_use_github_action()}} help a project meet the
checklist and keep meeting it.
}
